# Shared working tree

- Default to one writer in the existing checkout; reuse warm services.
- Extra writers require authorized parallel work, disjoint whole-file ownership,
  stable shared interfaces, and one coordinator for Git and shared processes.
  Respect project.json maxWriters when adopted; it grants no spawn permission.
- Leave edits unstaged until a commit is requested. The coordinator checkpoints
  a coherent, dependency-complete batch of ready files via
  `committing-on-shared-trunk`; unfinished or unrelated WIP stays out.
- Never stash, reset/clean WIP, globally format, or kill shared processes as
  housekeeping. No automatic per-task branch/worktree/PR lifecycle.
- On unexpected overlapping edits, pause affected work and reconcile ownership;
  continue independent work. Ask only if ownership cannot be resolved.
- Use .loadout/engineering/WORKFLOW.md when adopted. Existing project requirements
  and authorization still apply; resolve conflicts before the affected action.
